{"r":4,"c":[[54,"The HDC1080 operates only as a slave device on the I2C bus interface. It is not allowed to have on the I2C bus"]]}
{"r":5,"c":[[54,"multiple devices with the same address. Connection to the bus is made via the open-drain I/O lines, SDA, and"]]}
{"r":6,"c":[[54,"SCL. The SDA and SCL pins feature integrated spike-suppression filters and Schmitt triggers to minimize the"]]}
{"r":7,"c":[[54,"effects of input spikes and bus noise. After power-up, the sensor needs at most 15 ms, to be ready to start RH"]]}
{"r":8,"c":[[54,"and temperature measurement. During this power-up time the HDC1080 is only able to provide the content of the"]]}
{"r":9,"c":[[54,"serial number registers (0xFB to 0xFF) if requested. After the power-up the sensor is in the sleep mode until a"]]}
{"r":10,"c":[[54,"communication or measurement is performed. All data bytes are transmitted MSB first."]]}
